    <Node ToolID="1720">
      <GuiSettings Plugin="AlteryxGuiToolkit.TextBox.TextBox">
        <Position x="680" y="237" width="1044" height="276" />
      </GuiSettings>
      <Properties>
        <Configuration>
          <Text><![CDATA[CONNECTION INFORMATION

INPUTS:  
The majority of the Salesforce inputs use this connection string ->
odbc:DRIVER={SQL Server};DATABASE=salesforce backups;SERVER=NUSCLEVPDBAMP02;Trusted_Connection=yes

There is other inputs and the tool will identify in the container.  For example Users also has an input to get YCode for US10 reporting.  

Many inputs combine multiple Salesforce tables in the tool to get other information.  Please see each tool

OUTPUTS:
The majority of the outputs use this connection string ->
odbc:DRIVER={SQL Server};DATABASE=SF_DATASOURCES;SERVER=NUSCLEVPDBAMP02;Trusted_Connection=yes
]]></Text>
          <Font name="Arial" size="12" style="1" />
          <TextColor name="White" />
          <FillColor r="0" g="64" b="128" />
          <Shape shape="0" />
          <Justification Justification="4" />
        </Configuration>
        <Annotation DisplayMode="0">
          <Name />
          <DefaultAnnotationText />
          <Left value="False" />
        </Annotation>
      </Properties>
    </Node>
    <Node ToolID="1721">
      <GuiSettings Plugin="AlteryxGuiToolkit.TextBox.TextBox">
        <Position x="668" y="573" width="1044" height="240" />
      </GuiSettings>
      <Properties>
        <Configuration>
          <Text><![CDATA[WORKFLOW ORGANIZATION

Workflow organized to include a table and the transformation needed to get a Salesforce object table in useable format in a container.  Effort was made to only include necessary fields, alias fields, changing a data types, ect.  The outputs are contained in 2 different containers (container #1391 and #1432) so containers may be turned off for maintenance/troubleshooting/rework.  All inputs are within a container there are 34 inputs that require a connection string.  There are 26 outputs that require a connection string.  An output may be an input elsewhere in the workflow please trace the connection wire.


]]></Text>
          <Font name="Arial" size="12" style="1" />
          <TextColor name="White" />
          <FillColor r="0" g="64" b="128" />
          <Shape shape="0" />
          <Justification Justification="4" />
        </Configuration>
        <Annotation DisplayMode="0">
          <Name />
          <DefaultAnnotationText />
          <Left value="False" />
        </Annotation>
      </Properties>
    </Node>
    <Node ToolID="1738">
      <GuiSettings Plugin="AlteryxGuiToolkit.TextBox.TextBox">
        <Position x="2480" y="705" width="1164" height="141" />
      </GuiSettings>
      <Properties>
        <Configuration>
          <Text><![CDATA[OPPORTUNITY TRANSFORMATION

Please contact me for questions and explanation to the opportunity transformation. 

In Salesforce, we were not able to get formula fields when it comes to currency translation.  We came up with the process, using the ISO code First converting everything to USD then using this converting everything to EUR.  The rates are for USD exchange rates and not ZAR to EUR for example..
]]></Text>
          <Font name="Arial" size="12" style="0" />
          <TextColor name="White" />
          <FillColor r="0" g="64" b="128" />
          <Shape shape="0" />
          <Justification Justification="4" />
        </Configuration>
        <Annotation DisplayMode="0">
          <Name />
          <DefaultAnnotationText />
          <Left value="False" />
        </Annotation>
      </Properties>
    </Node>
